  {
    "id": 19,
    "question": "What are the biggest market risks for the next 12 months?",
    "stats": {
      "Los riesgos principales identificados son: (1) \"Valuation and concentration risks, and extreme euphoria\"; (2) \"Financial repression and fiscal dominance\"; (3) \"Geopolitical risks amid controlled disorder\" (en escenario downside 30%: \"Political instability, a de-anchoring of inflation expectations, tightening liquidity, credit events, or earnings/capex disappointments in a concentrated, expensive market could trigger a downturn\"). Además, 35% de profesionales ve \"Higher inflation\" como principal disrupción.": 1,
      "\"The age of speculation is giving way to real‑world results, but investors must be mindful that old challenges—valuation, inflation, and geopolitical uncertainty—remain firmly in play.\" También: \"Inflation remains an overarching risk... Geopolitical uncertainty—from trade tensions to the war in Ukraine—adds further complexity to the global outlook.\"": 1,
      "Los principales riesgos identificados son: (1) \"Bond yield spikes could pose a risk to this financing\" (spikes en yields de bonos), (2) \"A more leveraged system also creates vulnerabilities to shocks such as bond yield spikes tied to fiscal concerns or policy tensions between managing inflation and debt servicing costs,\" (3) Restricciones físicas: \"AI data centers could use 15-20% of current U.S. electricity demand by 2030...Rising power demand collides with a backlog of projects waiting to connect with the electric grid,\" (4) \"Retail flows into semi-liquid private credit products are likely to be pro-cyclical and may amplify volatility during periods of stress.\"": 1,
      "\"Despite fading market shocks, ongoing geopolitical tensions and elevated gold volatility signal that concerns about global risks may linger in 2026...the market-relevant potential for the largest short-term surprises stem from: the US-China trade and diplomatic front; Russian provocations and sabotage in Europe; US military confrontation in Latin America; a renewed war between Israel and Iran.\" Adicionalmente: \"An unexpected slowdown, especially among hyperscalers, could disrupt the market rally that has been rooted in earnings growth.\" \"US yields are close to the lower end of the range seen over the past twelve months...A correction in yields would not be that surprising.\" \"high and rising debt levels...are raising debt sustainability risks\"": 1,
      "\"Catalysts for  are weaker economic data, equity market volatility or evidence of growing credit stresses in either private or public markets... Tariffs and the impact of immigration controls on labour supply could combine to keep inflation higher for longer... Geographically, US markets are most at risk from any deviation from the benign core scenario... If growth also turns out to be weaker, investors could also focus on the US fiscal outlook, again widening spreads in the US rates and credit markets.\"": 1,
      "\"The biggest risk for investors remains the elevated starting point for risk assets, especially in the United States, and how offsides portfolios have been to the broadening of asset class returns underway\"": 1,
      "\"The global economic and political landscape is shifting rapidly, marked by a broad reordering of trade relations and political alliances around the globe. At the same time, fiscal sustainability and questions over central bank independence are top of mind.\" Tabla completa de riesgos en página 12.": 1,
      "\"Nevertheless, we remain mindful of policy and macro uncertainty. The US Federal Reserve could end its rate-cutting cycle sooner than expected, and data-centre construction could face delays due to labour shortages – not to mention the potential for escalating geopolitical tensions in any region.\"": 1,
      "Riesgos clave identificados por Goldman Sachs: (1) Labor market deterioration could trigger hard landing if sustained; (2) Tariff cost pass-through to consumers could depress spending; (3) Fiscal deficit concerns - \"pinpointing the exact moment when fiscal anxieties will emerge or peak is impossible\"; (4) Geopolitical escalation - \"Despite steps closer to peace in the Middle East, geopolitical risks remain high. Russia and Ukraine remain far apart\"; (5) AI capex sustainability - \"return on investment visibility remains low\"; (6) Market concentration risk - \"top 10 US companies represent ~40% of S&P 500's market cap\"; (7) Credit events and bank exposure to NDFIs; (8) Real estate stress - \"$57 billion of distressed assets in the US\" mainly office.": 1,
      "Los principales riesgos identificados son: (1) fragmentación global y volatilidad geopolítica, (2) inflación más alta que lo esperado, (3) incertidumbre sobre independencia de la FED, (4) concentración de mercado en tecnología/AI, (5) deterioro adicional en el mercado laboral, (6) monetización incierta de AI": 1,
      "Los mayores riesgos incluyen: (1) inestabilidad del mercado laboral estadounidense con posibles layoffs acelerados, (2) corrección del mercado de acciones del 20%+ que podría desencadenar pérdidas de crédito, (3) impingement en la independencia de la FED, (4) riesgos fiscales si los ingresos por aranceles caen, (5) impacto negativo de IA en empleo, y (6) geopolítica (guerra en Ucrania, tensiones US-China).": 1,
      "Los mayores riesgos incluyen: (1) erosión de instituciones de EE.UU. y pérdida de confianza en el dólar, (2) corrección en mercados de IA tras inversión especulativa, (3) fragmentación política (Hungría, Francia, posible reforma Fed), (4) escalada de conflictos por \"chokepoints\" (rareza de tierras, semiconductores), (5) insostenibilidad fiscal de Francia y riesgos de crisis de bonos, (6) divergencia en economía de EE.UU. entre AI \"haves\" y Main Street creando vulnerabilidades": 1,
      "\"While political headlines will remain front and center in 2026, history suggests their impact on financial markets is often short-lived. However, there are risks that could bring markets back to earth in the year ahead, including: 1) a potential disappointment in AI progress or adoption, 2) a resurgence or persistence of inflation, 3) a more entrenched phase of US-China strategic rivalry, and 4) the (re-) emergence of sovereign or private sector debt concerns.\"": 1,
      "Table 2 lista: \"1. US recession due to a breaking rather than bending labor market; 2. A high-pressure global economy and captured Fed; 3. AI ecosystem implosion, gold crash; 4. Renewed trade-related uncertainty (Supreme court rulings, US-China deal breakdown); 5. European NATO member calls in Article 5; 6. The potential for systemic events stemming from private (credit) markets\"": 1
